sqlsmith
------------------------------------------
SQLsmith is a random SQL query generator. Its paragon is Csmith, which proved
valuable for quality assurance in C compilers.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libboost_regex1.66-1.66.0-1
  libgcc1-14.4.0-1
  libpq5-18.6-1
  libpqxx4.0-4.0.1-1
  libsqlite3_0-3.49.1-1
  libstdc++6-14.4.0-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  autoconf-20260320-3
  autoconf-archive-2024.10.16-1
  automake-20260320-2
  binutils-2.47-1
  cygport-0.37.12-1
  gcc-g++-14.4.0-1
  libboost-devel-1.66.0-1
  libpq-devel-18.6-1
  libpq5-18.6-1
  libpqxx-devel-4.0.1-1
  libsqlite3-devel-3.49.1-1
  make-4.4.1-2

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/anse1/sqlsmith

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/anse1/sqlsmith/archive/refs/tags/v1.5.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack sqlsmith-1.5-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./sqlsmith-1.5-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/sqlsmith-1.5-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/sqlsmith-1.5-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

Files included in the binary package:

(sqlsmith)
  /usr/bin/sqlsmith.exe
  /usr/share/doc/Cygwin/sqlsmith.README
  /usr/share/doc/sqlsmith/COPYING
